  "summary": "The Oaklandside published unedited candidate questionnaire responses from 2026 Oakland mayoral and City Council candidates on issues including whether to renew the city's two-year Flock Safety ALPR contract approved in December. Candidates split: Grisham and Pechenuk back renewal, Lee and Robinson condition renewal on independent review and privacy safeguards, Adams and Wang oppose or seek alternatives to Flock, and Sidebotham expresses concern about data sharing.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I do not support the City contracting with Flock and oppose renewal. I oppose this use of mass surveillance for which the effectiveness is unknown but the harms are well documented, and I oppose working with an unethical business like Flock that has provided data to ICE.",
      "paragraph_idx": 68
    },
    {
      "quote": "I authored what officials have called the strongest safeguards in the country: \"hard coding off\" the National Lookup feature that gave federal backdoor access; banning the use for enforcement related to immigration, abortions, or gender-affirming care; requiring security audits every 6 months to affirm that safeguards; setting the nation's highest fines at $200k per violation.",
      "paragraph_idx": 82
    },
    {
      "quote": "I am now working to ensure we share data with only Sanctuary cities... Now, I am actively pushing the city for an open bid to replace Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 82
    },
    {
      "quote": "I will support flock cameras 100% as I have in the past and would push for renewing the system.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    },
    {
      "quote": "I would support renewing Flock's contract only if an independent review demonstrates public-safety value and effective privacy protections.",
      "paragraph_idx": 50
    }
  ],
